  "notes": "{間|ま}もなく means \"soon\" or \"shortly\"—more formal than もうすぐ.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {間|ま}もなく: soon, shortly (formal)\n- もうすぐ: soon (casual)\n- すぐ: immediately, right away\n- そのうち: before long, sometime (vague)\n\nCOMMON CONTEXTS:\nOften heard in public announcements:\n- {間|ま}もなく{電車|でんしゃ}が{参|まい}ります (The train will arrive shortly)\n- {間|ま}もなく{開演|かいえん}です (The show will begin shortly)\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nLiterally \"without interval\" ({間|ま} = interval + もなく = without).",
